{
  "dom_id": "step-q224526",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the binomial random variable $X∼B(6,0.48)$ given below, compute $P(X=3).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0198\\,$ | $\\,0.1293\\,$ | $\\,0.3820\\,$ | $\\,0.6930\\,$ | $\\,0.9083\\,$ | $\\,0.9878\\,$ | $\\,1.0000\\,$ |\n\n$P(X=3)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(3) & =P(X\\le 3) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2,3\\}) \\\\  & =P(X\\in \\{0,1,2\\})+P(X=3) \\\\  & =P(X\\le 2)+P(X=3) \\\\  & =F(2)+P(X=3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=3) & =F(3)-F(2) \\\\  & =0.6930-0.3820 \\\\  & =0.3110.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
